reliable4 ITEM A transient-start gate: 20 jobs with --retries 2 whose cmd.Start()
fails with ENOEXEC every time (a bare-name 'newgrp' on the runner's PATH that is executable
but not a valid executable format), on an isolated dev manager (-s local, --max_cores 2,
--runner_filelog). ENOEXEC is deliberately TRANSIENT, so these are released, not buried at once.
Gate: buried == 20 AND execAttempts == 60 (jobs*(retries+1)) AND all 20 give
'command failed to start' as their problem.
Pre-fix: buried == 0 and attempts climb past 60 without bound (UntilBuried never decrements
for a job that never reported a start, so the retry ceiling is never reached).
A MISSING measurement (no runner logs, 0 attempts, dead manager) is a FAIL, not a PASS.
